<p>Governments across Europe and beyond are organizing charter flights and other help to bring home citizens stranded by the sharp disruption to air travel caused by the Middle East war triggered by U.S.-Israeli attacks on Iran. The United Kingdom said it chartered its first repatriation flight for Britons and also plans to deploy a Royal Navy warship to the eastern Mediterranean to bolster security around its Royal Air Force base at Akrotiri in Cyprus. France’s first charter jet has brought nationals home, and officials said more repatriation flights were planned for March 4. Airlines have begun limited resumptions from some Gulf hubs after days of widespread cancellations, but the picture remains uneven, with many routes shifting to avoid closed or risky airspace. Aviation analytics firm Cirium counted at least 12,903 flight cancellations from Saturday through Monday—about 40% of planned flights. Based on the region’s typical seat capacity, Cirium estimates the disruption may already have affected more than a million travelers. Even with uncertainty still hanging over schedules, the gradual return of some services—and the growing number of government-organized flights—has given many stranded passengers a practical way home.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/I-69oCdcVKklXB8n8VHXOnllJXVtTpPc2phxXrAKiYsgB9vyMH3T7AQW6Z-Odnk92gr_tMAgzlvZJ-X4e1EGbTWptw1lqUexKvJZ7Qt6' alt='A passenger gestures upon arrival at the airport in Frankfurt, Germany, from Dubai.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Uneven restart: After near-total UAE cancellations on Sunday, Dubai and Abu Dhabi only resumed operations in a limited way, leaving many passengers dependent on sporadic flights and rebookings.</li><li>Route avoidance: Flightradar24 data cited by Dawn showed several Emirates departures turning south soon after takeoff, underscoring carriers’ efforts to steer clear of closed or risky airspace.</li><li>Who was flying: During the tentative resumption, Dawn reported that only some flights by Emirates, low-cost flydubai and Russia’s Aeroflot were operating, while numerous Royal Jordanian flights continued in and out of Amman.</li><li>Evacuation outcomes: As limited commercial service returned and governments arranged charters, Al-Monitor reported relieved passengers arriving in countries including Australia, France, Germany, India, Russia and Taiwan.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>UK government: The UK announced its first charter repatriation flight and said it will deploy a Royal Navy warship to the eastern Mediterranean to bolster security around the RAF base at Akrotiri in Cyprus. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/uk-charters-first-repatriation-flight-for-british-stranded-due-to-west-asia-conflict/article70703088.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>French foreign ministry: Foreign Minister Jean-Noel Barrot said the first charter jet brought French nationals home and that additional repatriation flights were planned for March 4, including for vulnerable people via chartered flights. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/first-charter-jet-brings-french-nationals-home-from-middle-east'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Qatar authorities: Qatar said it blocked Iranian attacks on its airport, a major regional hub, as airspace closures and security risks continued to complicate civilian aviation. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1978051/special-flights-to-evacuate-travellers-stranded-in-middle-east'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Stranded passengers: Travelers described sleepless nights and days-long efforts to leave the region after the war erupted, as flights restarted only gradually from hubs such as Dubai and Riyadh. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/new-flights-evacuate-travellers-stranded-middle-east-war'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/uk-charters-first-repatriation-flight-for-british-stranded-due-to-west-asia-conflict/article70703088.ece'>U.K. charters first repatriation flight for British stranded due to West Asia conflict</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/03/world/middleeast/iran-war-middle-east-traveler-evacuations.html'>Western Governments Rush to Help Stranded Travelers in the Middle East</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/new-flights-evacuate-travellers-stranded-middle-east-war'>New flights evacuate travellers stranded by Middle East war</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/first-charter-jet-brings-french-nationals-home-from-middle-east'>First charter jet brings French nationals home from Middle East</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1978051/special-flights-to-evacuate-travellers-stranded-in-middle-east'>Special flights to evacuate travellers stranded in Middle East</a> - dawn.com</li></ul>